+**Recompute only what changed.** Each child record's replay is cached by the file's own signature (size and modified time; `ref_scope` in `page_tools.js`, `Task.ref_scope`). When one child's file changes, only that child is replayed again; the parent's totals (progress, completion, counts) are still added up fresh on every read from the children it holds. Time to answer `{"summary":{}}` on session-e00f55c9 (101 child records) right after one child file changed: about 115-130 ms before, 12-20 ms after. Test: `node Servex/agents/ref-cache.test.mjs`.
+
+**Completion at once, for any session.** `item({path: "/framework/ai/sessions/<uuid>/", delta: {"completion": {}}})`, or the dated folder's url, answers `{ok: true, answer: {completion: {done, total, stopped, completion}}}`: the tally of its tasks' current states and the number. It only reads and writes nothing. It works for a past session too, as long as its folder holds a record; a folder with no record is refused, and nothing is written. On session-e00f55c9: `{done: 30, total: 132, stopped: 74, completion: 0.227}`.
+
